  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Capture Contract",
      "type": "text",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "# Saga Thesis Capture Template\n\nUse this dashboard only for Bab IV focused panel screenshots. Set an absolute run window, then filter `suite_label`, `pattern`, `scenario`, and `run_label` before every capture. Prefer panel fullscreen/kiosk or panel share images; do not capture the full dashboard page.\n\nBab IV figure filenames: evidence preflight -> `grafana-bab4-evidence-health.png`; overview stats -> `grafana-bab4-overview-stats.png`; throughput -> `grafana-bab4-throughput-panel.png`; client P95 latency -> `grafana-bab4-latency-panel.png`; compensation lifecycle -> `grafana-bab4-compensation-lifecycle.png`; contention correctness -> `grafana-bab4-contention-correctness.png`; recovery sequence -> `grafana-bab4-recovery-sequence.png`; resource support -> `grafana-bab4-resource-network.png`; root-cause step latency -> `grafana-bab4-step-latency.png`; trace waterfall -> `grafana-bab4-trace-waterfall.png`; profile -> `grafana-bab4-profile.png`.\n\nRecommended focused captures: overview stats -> panels 2, 3, 4, 5, 17, 18; throughput -> panel 6; client P95 latency -> panel 7; recovery sequence -> panels 8 and 9 with the resilience suite_label and run_label order visible; resource support -> panels 10 and 11 only; root-cause step latency -> panel 14; throughput speedup and P95 delta -> panels 19 and 20; contention correctness -> panel 21; compensation lifecycle -> panel 22; evidence preflight -> panel 16.\n\nCapture purpose per filename: evidence health must prove the sources are alive before reading results; overview stats must place iteration, terminal status, outcome match, and timeout in one window; throughput and latency must use the same scenario window so rate and P95 are compared together; compensation lifecycle must show failed scenarios after business effects exist; contention correctness must pair raw rate with terminal success and request failure; recovery sequence must preserve the failure-recovery-recovery-failure order through run_label ordering; resource support must show CPU and memory concentration only; step latency must separate participant work from coordination work. Use one figure for one analytical point. Keep labels/time windows in notes, not visible thesis prose.",
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        }
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.1.1"
    },
    {
